WEBVTT

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.150
Erin, I'll be returning home on
our anniversary next month.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.860
This time, I promise I'll be home.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.830
About your birthday a little while
ago... Are you still mad at me?

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:02.800
A little while ago? It was three months ago.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.800
What the hell have you been
doing for three months?!

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.300
I already explained it to you, didn't I?

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.670
Because of the submersion
accident in the 4th block...

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:15.310
First of all, how many times did
you come home this year?

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.680
Twice! Just twice!

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.780
On top of that, one time was for only five hours!

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:21.450
Honey, please listen to me!

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.520
I don't need any more excuses!

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.350
Hey...

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:35.260
First of all, how many times did
you come home this year?

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.530
Twice! Just twice!

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:22.100
Get out of my way, boomer!

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.870
Walking in the middle of the road,
what do you think you are?!

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:31.470
What? I'm gonna call the
AD Police if you touch me!

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.420
Don't stare at me!

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.120
Well, I'm going to try it on.

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.430
It's cold!

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.700
The coolant is still being adjusted.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.100
Please be a little patient.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:08.740
This is great! It's a lot lighter than before!

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:14.190
Look at me, Sylia! I can move
much easier than before!

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.460
When I wear this, I won't be inferior to Priss!

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.080
You've come here again.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:24.700
Because of him, tuning will be far faster.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.000
He has a knack for it.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.940
Mackey, I don't want you to get
involved with this place.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.370
I want you to be ordinary.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:37.440
Yes, be an ordinary boy.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.810
What we're doing has nothing to do with you.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:47.150
She's right. Nigel is a special exception,

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:50.660
but the Knight Sabers are a team just for girls.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:51.780
Right, Sylia?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:05.140
There are no clothes here that you
can wear, Mr. Mackey.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.470
I guess so.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.980
Mr. Meisio, how long have
you been working here?

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:13.910
Since Miss Sylia came back to Tokyo.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:18.010
Because she saved my life.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:25.330
I wonder if I should stay here or not?

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.560
Why do you say things like that?

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.030
I'm sorry. I said something
that I shouldn't have!

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.330
I'm sorry. I followed you without asking.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:19.080
Is it okay?

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:22.350
Well, Sylia went out somewhere so...

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:26.050
It's incredible! Did you make
this yourself, Nigel?

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:27.690
It isn't finished yet.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.280
It's a wonderful job to be able
to make things like this!

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.030
Genom is scheduled to complete
the Showhamm Project soon,

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:40.170
which will solve the chronic shortages of energy.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.270
With the progress of this project,

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:46.110
the international stock price of
Genom Corp. is rising suddenly.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:47.400
In the London stock market...

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.170
Every time I go out of town,

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:17.000
it makes me sick to see that
stupid umbrella in the sky.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.140
I'm sorry to make you come to a place like this.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:24.280
The boomers working on the Sky
Hook will be trashed soon, right?

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:28.250
The chairman has no intention
of slowing or stopping production.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:30.650
As a matter of fact, he's planning
to increase production.

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:33.120
Does he still want to increase
the number of boomers?

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.660
Recovery from the quake
is already complete!

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:37.920
It's for developing frontier planets.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:41.800
The next target will be the natural
resources of Jupiter and Saturn.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:44.770
He's conducting experiments on
boomers in the Atlantic

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:48.170
which will be able to function
in severe environments.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:49.870
In the deep sea?

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:54.740
Pressure and such are similar to
planets with high gravity.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:56.880
Continue.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:00.150
This experimental boomer, which
is incapable of making decisions,

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:03.050
is called a remote slave type,
and its common name is Moto.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:05.290
I already know that!

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.920
I'm sorry.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.220
I have to remember your application for this.

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:11.690
That's none of your business!

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.930
What happened to the Moto?
Has it gotten out of control?

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:20.300
It's not clear yet. It seems one of
them has appeared in Tokyo.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.870
My section is very upset, and
we're currently searching for it.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.540
The Moto isn't able to move by itself.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.010
Where's the reflector that's
supposed to operate it?

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:30.240
We're not certain.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:34.110
Communications with the deep
sea facility have been cut.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.420
What would happen if a boomer
with such abilities

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:38.650
came to the surface and went insane?

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:43.190
It's not armored, but it's equipped
for harsh environments,

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:45.560
so it's like a walking fortress.

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.690
Contact me again if you find anything out.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.210
Liar...

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:22.600
The Moto in the experimental facility?

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:23.930
Are you saying that the Moto

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:27.230
has come to Tokyo on its own, and
been walking around for a month?

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:28.500
It's too ridiculous!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:32.210
The name of the reflector is Bill
Nordberg, he's an engineer.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:34.940
He's the only one who can operate it.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:39.850
The Moto probably appeared in
Tokyo because his wife lives here.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.080
I see.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:45.750
There are some civilians who've
already called the AD Police.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:49.750
Good job. Let them take care of it, I guess.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:08.070
It's wandering around town.

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:11.770
Linna's suit isn't complete yet,
so you and Priss are going.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:14.010
What's wrong?

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.410
This neighborhood's unsafe if there's
a strange boomer like that.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:21.940
Bill, did you come home?

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:31.890
What are you talking about?

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:34.950
Your husband's at the bottom of
the Atlantic as always, isn't he?

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:41.940
He's not inside.

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:44.630
Are you okay? I guess the boomer's gone.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:47.970
That was Bill.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.710
We're looking for the reflector.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:52.180
The only person who can stop
the boomer is your husband.

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:55.650
Excuse me, but can I leave now?

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:59.490
Sure. I've already finished verifying your identity.

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:00.890
If you'll excuse me...

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.060
Bill...

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:10.190
I'm sorry, but let me borrow this.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:18.300
Bill's come back to see me.

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:23.980
A boomer is at large. This is a
mission for all PC's in the area.

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:26.110
As soon as you find it, force
it to cease all activity.

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:30.980
The target is a remote boomer for
work in harsh environments.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:33.050
I want to go with you.

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:36.520
Well, leave things to us today.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:37.760
Right, Priss?

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.860
Please don't disturb me.

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:43.730
Nigel has finished tuning my suit,
so I'm different than what I was.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:49.940
The AD Police say they've lost
the target. It's time to go.

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:51.200
Priss, is anything wrong?

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:54.270
No, no. Nothing.

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:58.710
I will confirm with Nigel about your
suit, Priss, but I'm sure it's done.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:01.180
Linna, you're going with me in the
mobile pit to support them.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:02.310
Right.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.720
The adjustments haven't been finished...

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:11.720
Let's go.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.600
I wonder why they're taking so long?

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:26.240
That woman said something strange, didn't she?

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:30.570
Her conscience drove her crazy!
She brought a man into the house.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:33.580
No, it's a little strange.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:37.880
First, the call from that civilian is suspicious.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:39.050
What's suspicious about it?

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:42.290
I think Genom is hiding something.

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:43.880
Where is this place?

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.130
A hydraulic gauge?

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.420
In the deep sea...

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:53.890
Boomer for High Pressure...
An experimental facility!

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:57.460
What's the matter?

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:26.530
Redial.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:30.770
You've reached the Nordberg residence.

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:34.670
We are not available right now.
Please leave a message.

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:40.450
Honey, I forgot to tell you I'll be
on vacation for three weeks,

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:43.820
starting with our anniversary.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.840
Why don't we relax a while, just you and me.

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:58.030
Nigel! Nigel! I know you're in there!

00:14:58.030 --> 00:15:00.500
Nigel! Nigel!

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:17.620
Nigel!

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:21.620
The Knight Sabers have...

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:25.460
Priss and the others have
dispatched with their hard suits!

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:29.550
They can do as they like. I didn't
tell them the suits were ready.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:32.900
Don't you care?

00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:36.770
None of my business. My job is to
maintain and set up the suits.

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:39.770
But I have to tell Sylia about
it as soon as possible!

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:41.430
That's broken.

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:45.610
It's already transformed!

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:47.580
Priss, Nene, are you there yet?

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.280
We've just arrived!

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:53.990
Let me go first!

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:54.890
Nene!

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:55.490
I can do it!
Nene!

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:56.610
I can do it!

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.430
I see...

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:13.740
I did it!

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:14.710
Nene!

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:41.970
It's connected to the net now.

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:44.170
Sylia! Sylia!

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.900
Priss' hard suit isn't ready yet!

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:54.010
I found the security tape at the
deep sea experimental facility.

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:55.620
Is this Bill?

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:56.910
Yeah...

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.020
Bill a month ago.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:00.850
What?
Bill a month ago.

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:01.520
What?
The last picture left in the tape is
this one, taken one month ago.

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:05.530
The last picture left in the tape is
this one, taken one month ago.

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:08.120
It means that right after this,
something's going to happen.

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:17.400
What the...

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:18.710
An accident.

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:21.440
Hey, then who the hell is operating
that thing now?!

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:50.030
Priss, hurry up and get back here!

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:53.970
If you say so, but at this very moment?

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:00.570
Here goes.

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:05.850
Damn!

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:06.450
Priss!
Damn!

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:07.350
Priss!
My arm, I can't move my arm!

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.150
My arm, I can't move my arm!

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:10.660
Oh, my God! It's my fault!

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:12.230
What's going to happen to Priss?!

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:13.920
Damn you!

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:18.890
Damn! I need my arm!

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:23.870
Priss, you can move your left
arm a little, can't you?

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.970
Shoot your right shoulder joint
with your left knuckle bomb!

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:29.380
The shock will restart the circuit.

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:30.670
Mackey...

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:35.420
Decrease the power of the knuckle
bomb to gauge three.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:39.020
It's my rule to not intervene
in these ladies' actions.

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:41.590
Remember, this is a special exception.

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:42.690
Thank you!

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:44.160
I understand, but...

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:57.840
Bill! You are Bill, aren't you?!

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:58.600
It's too dangerous!

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:00.470
You came home for me, didn't you?!

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:01.940
Bill!

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:05.040
That's a boomer!

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:09.280
Ms. Erin! Your husband died in
an accident a month ago!

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:14.090
All right!

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:47.490
It's okay.

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:51.960
Even if he was alive, he had
no intention of coming home.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:55.090
I think he really intended to
come home this time.

00:19:56.760 --> 00:20:00.600
Your husband took three weeks
vacation starting today.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:09.280
And he made reservations for two
to go to an island in the south.

00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:11.710
Departure date is tomorrow.

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:16.580
Your husband also ordered this.

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:31.530
I know he wanted to bring that
home and see your happy face.

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:34.730
If he was alive...

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:58.980
Next Episode

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:05.180
A live stage, the eyes of the
band members meet.

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:06.950
Along with the noise of
the mic feedback,

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:11.190
a rough reflection echoes
loudly in the hall.

00:21:11.190 --> 00:21:13.490
A strong beat begins to radiate.

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:15.230
When the stage turns to red,

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:17.700
a spotlight aims at a little shadow.

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:19.960
That's me.

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:22.230
Next Bubblegum Crisis!
